  "summary": "Release publication and portability correction, document group 2 of 3.",
  "why": "GitHub run 34281992115 exposes unpublished capture-evidence commits, platform-dependent PNG compression and Python 3.10 UTC-Z parsing in the existing supplier helper. The existing evidence tag is now published; all 354 commit references resolve from inspected public refs. No historical ledger reference changes. CI preflights ledger/integration before pytest. Fixture generator v3 uses specified RGB8/filter-0/stored-block PNG bytes; all 10 changed images preserve pixels and source PDFs stay unchanged. Library dependencies, Core src and ontology bytes do not change. UTC parser normalization retains original ledger text. Six encoder/CI RED cases turn GREEN; 79 status/OCR/CI tests pass; the supplier replay parser RED turns GREEN. The observed remote Python 3.12 suite alone takes 27m44s, so main/release test jobs allow 45 minutes for existing setup and docs too. No test/platform is removed. Final clean full/package and remote checks remain required; new Re-entry integration stays excluded.",
